    "body": "Impacted versions: 13.0\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce:\r\n1. Login to the latest runbot 13.0 with the administrator user \r\n2. Go to Settings > Users and change the notification type from \"Handle by Emails\" to \"Handle in Odoo\" for the user \"Marc Demo\". Give the user \"Administrator\" rights on the sales app for easier testing.\r\n2. Create  a new quotation for `Deco Addict`, add some line on the quote and either e-mail the customer or add him as a follower on the quote.\r\n3. Log an internal note to `Marc Demo` (with an @ to Marc so he gets a message).\r\n4. Login with the user `Marc Demo` and open the messages from the top. You'll see a message from `Mitchel Admin` with the message:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6352350/74220425-e0a32f00-4caf-11ea-9d5a-690ca1f9d590.png)\r\n5. Reply on this message with something like \"Yes this is true\":\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6352350/74220449-f1ec3b80-4caf-11ea-82fc-825eaacba156.png)\r\n6. Logout and login with `Mitchel Admin` again and now go back to this order. Now look at the history of the chatter:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6352350/74220543-2f50c900-4cb0-11ea-80cd-df2049ca677c.png)\r\n\r\n\r\nCurrent behavior:\r\nThe reply that was done by `Marc Demo` didn't keep track of the message type. The reply has become a normal reply which is emailed to all followers.\r\n\r\nExpected behavior:\r\nAs the ping was an internal message from somebody internal to somebody internal the reply from the chatter on this message should also become an internal note. Now the customer is emailed with internal communication which can potential hold important internal information not meant for the customer.\r\n\r\n",
